nd reinforced concrete structure faced with buff brick. The name was given because most of the early tenants were associated with the petroleum industry.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"Petroleum Building (Tulsa)","photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Petroleum_Building_Tulsa_00.png/1280px-Petroleum_Building_Tulsa_00.png","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Petroleum_Building_Tulsa_00.png/500px-Petroleum_Building_Tulsa_00.png","w":1200,"h":1388,"author":"0x0077BE","license":"CC0","licenseUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/deed.en","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Petroleum_Building_Tulsa_00.png"}},{"id":"tulsa_oaklawn_cemetery","areaId":"tulsa","name":"Oaklawn Cemetery","category":"park","tags":["history","photo"],"location":{"lat":36.1486,"lng":-95.9775},"visitMinutes":45,"priceLevel":0,"photoSeed":"tulsa_oaklawn_cemetery","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":8,"commonsNearby":8,"wikiPageviews":38,"wikidataSitelinks":2,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-20"},"hashtags":["oaklawncemetery","tulsa"],"bestLight":"morning","summary":"Oaklawn Cemetery is the oldest existing cemetery in Tulsa, Oklahoma.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"Oaklawn Cemetery (Tulsa)","photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Oaklawn_Cemetery_gates_Tulsa_OK_2025-12-04_12-57-04.jpg/1280px-Oaklawn_Cemetery_gates_Tulsa_OK_2025-12-04_12-57-04.jpg","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Oaklawn_Cemetery_gates_Tulsa_OK_2025-12-04_12-57-04.jpg/500px-Oaklawn_Cemetery_gates_Tulsa_OK_2025-12-04_12-57-04.jpg","w":1200,"h":675,"author":"G. Edward Johnson","license":"CC BY 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Oaklawn_Cemetery_gates_Tulsa_OK_2025-12-04_12-57-04.jpg"}},{"id":"tulsa_southwestern_bell_main_dial_building","areaId":"tulsa","name":"Southwestern Bell M